From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: D8-LINUX-6 <d8-linux@flyweb.invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sync account: "computer" instead of "Mac"; a real model on Linux

The sync account joins Macs and Linux computers, so its 41 strings say
"computer" (es and es-419: "equipo") on every platform. Message names do not
change; the es and es-419 translations move to the new grit ids.

DeviceModel(): Mac exactly as before. On Linux HardwareModelName() is empty
(the 3.2.2-50 sent the fallback "Mac"), so LinuxModel() reads, once, a model
like the Macs' "MacPro6,1": the DMI product name with a short vendor (MSI,
ASUS, Lenovo...), or the board when the product name is only a code inside it
("MSI B760 GAMING PLUS WIFI MS-7D98"), Lenovo's product_version, then the CPU
model, then "Linux". Placeholders are skipped. Never serial numbers, UUIDs or
the machine name (MOTOR-47).

Base: brave-core 583b882d52b20d710afbaa4fa31934c7d02cb1fa with the working tree 57132d0746 (U3 final, 0012, 6, 7,
Linux icons, desktop and #1250); result tree e8f182a1e3.
